Practical: Install Docker and deploy a two-page E-commerce website
Aim: To install Docker and deploy an E-commerce web application consisting of at least two web pages.

Software required: Windows, Docker Desktop, PowerShell, HTML and Nginx.
Step 1: Install Docker Desktop
1. Open Docker Desktop's official website.
2. Download Docker Desktop for Windows.
3. Run the installer and follow the instructions.
4. Start Docker Desktop and wait until the Docker engine is running.
Open PowerShell and check Docker:
docker --version
docker info


If these commands work without a Docker engine connection error, continue.
Step 2: Create the project folder
Run these commands one at a time in PowerShell:
mkdir "$HOME\development\docker-ecommerce" -Force


cd "$HOME\development\docker-ecommerce"


This creates the folder where we will store all our website files.
Step 3: Create the Home page
Run:
notepad index.html


Paste this code into Notepad:

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>ShopEasy Home</title>
</head>
<body style="font-family: Arial; text-align: center;">
    <h1>Welcome to ShopEasy</h1>
    <p>Your online shopping website</p>

    <a href="/">Home</a> |
    <a href="/products.html">Products</a>

    <h2>Featured Products</h2>

    <h3>Headphones - ₹1499</h3>
    <button onclick="alert('Added to cart!')">Add to Cart</button>

    <h3>Smart Watch - ₹2499</h3>
    <button onclick="alert('Added to cart!')">Add to Cart</button>
</body>
</html>



Save with Ctrl + S and close Notepad.

This is our first web page.
Step 4: Create the Products page
Run:
notepad products.html


Paste this code:

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>ShopEasy Products</title>
</head>
<body style="font-family: Arial; text-align: center;">
    <h1>Our Products</h1>

    <a href="/">Home</a> |
    <a href="/products.html">Products</a>

    <h2>Available Products</h2>

